Original commit body from 3ed1a807d789af33f0886824b692728bfabfa748:

`store.session().invalidateAndCancel()` names no receiver variable, so
`_extract_call_target` reported the chain head and every such site took the
`external` placeholder -- while the SAME call one binding apart
(`let s = store.session(); s.invalidateAndCancel()`) has been typed through the
return-type registry since PR #760. One catalogued sink, reachable in one
spelling and unmatchable in the other.

One walker now answers the receiver-expression family by mechanism rather than
by example: a call result (recursively, so `a.b().c().d()` is walked), a
constructor, a cast, a parenthesised expression, and any of those under `try` /
`await`. A parenthesised tuple and a cast to a collection are not receiver types
and stay untyped. `_swift_call_result_type` delegates to the same walker, so a
chained or `try`-wrapped INITIALISER is typed by the one rule too.

Reading every moved row back against Alamofire source found two producer defects
this amplified, both fixed where the fact is registered rather than where it is
read:

  * `-> Self` was registered literally and put a module of `Self` on 76 sites --
    a present-but-wrong hint, INV-kotob's defect under a new spelling. It names
    the enclosing type, and now resolves to it.
  * a generic PARAMETER return (`func pick<U>() -> U`) names nothing at a call
    site and is refused. A constrained parameter's BOUND (`<V: Codable>`) is
    still a real type.

MEASURED, per call site, both arms in one process:

  Alamofire         10,699 sites   330 changed   322 gains   0 losses   0 re-keys
  VernissageServer  12,544 sites   114 changed   112 gains   0 losses   2 re-keys

The 322 gains are 286 project types into `receiver_type_hint`, 21 external types
into the module slot, and 8 calls that now resolve to project methods. Both
Vernissage re-keys are a local shadowing a same-named parameter, which the
per-function scope map cannot separate: one of the pair is corrected, the other
regressed. A B1-vs-B2 read-back of the producer fixes finds 78 sites losing a
module slot on Alamofire and all 78 are `Self` / `U` corrections -- non-Self/U
losses: 0.

io-boundaries are UNCHANGED on both (Alamofire 40 edges / 30 chains,
VernissageServer 8 / 8). That is the honest negative result: the gains are
overwhelmingly project types, which ADR-0051 keeps out of the module slot by
design, and no external gain lands on a catalogued method-kind row these
repositories call.

Also restores coverage of the ERROR-node type-recovery path. Its fixture stopped
reaching it when the grammar went 0.0.1 -> 0.7.3 (PR #763, which changed
pyproject.toml and so never measured swift.py's coverage): 0.7.3 parses that
class cleanly and the test still passed, because it asserts the class is FOUND
and it is now found by the ordinary path. The path is not dead -- 246 of
VernissageServer's 263 error-parsing files carry a type keyword in an ERROR node
-- so it is pinned with the delta-debugged minimum of one of them.

